                <pb facs="1149" n="1139" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg1139"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.801/9–2949: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in the
                        United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Douglas</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-09-29T13:00:00-05:00">September 29,
                            1949—1 p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3545. At request Dept, Brit Emb last week requested FonOff to tele copy Brit
                    protest re Chi Nat Govt seizure SS <hi rendition="#italic">Edith Moller</hi>
                    ex-Shanghai. Nats have now intercepted three Amer-flag Isbrandtsen ships outside
                    Shanghai. In view desirability knowing Brit line of action, pls indicate FonOff
                    urgency our interest this question.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Webb</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
